I am in the museum's small cafeteria.
The weather is very cold right now.
I go to the counter.
"Bhaiya, please give me one cutting chai."
I take my tea and sit near the window.
I look outside.
It is raining heavily again.
These drops look beautiful.
An older woman is sitting at the next table.
She looks at the rain and smiles.
"This rain is not stopping today," she says.
I smile and reply.
"Yes, the weather changes very quickly here."
"Have you come here before as well?" she asks.
"No, I have come to this museum for the first time."
"I came to Mumbai five months ago."
"At that time the weather was completely dry."
She laughs.
"Now you are seeing the real Mumbai."
I drink my hot tea and look at those clouds.
